-- Atomic private research preservation from 18 exact Harley guide sources.
-- 40 source-captured sections: 18 buying, 16 history, 5 technical, 1 generation.
-- All content remains draft/unverified. Does NOT alter any public page, stock,
-- catalogue identity or editorial rights. Only plain-text source excerpts.
DO $$
DECLARE source_rows integer; inserted integer; existing integer;
BEGIN
 SELECT count(*) INTO source_rows FROM (VALUES
 (143,16,'Used buying guidance','road-glide','d9ed17e761080d2076bdd138581f4083cdbd9b6e','buying_guidance','UK buyer''s model-specific checklist','Confirm whether it is Road Glide, Road Glide Special, Road Glide Ultra or a CVO variant. Check fairing alignment and whether audio, screen and handlebar modifications are original. Inspect hard panniers, latches, touring electrical equipment and evidence of crash damage. These are suggested inspection points rather than a substitute for a qualified mechanical inspection, HPI checks or verifying export documents.'),
 (143,3,'Model history and production context','road-glide','d9ed17e761080d2076bdd138581f4083cdbd9b6e','chronology','Detailed model generations and factory references','Different year-and-trim versions can have different engine families, chassis and touring equipment. These two documented reference points help identify the correct motorcycle before requesting UK supply. 2017 Road Glide Ultra (FLTRU) The factory''s 2017 Road Glide Ultra specification records a Twin-Cooled Milwaukee-Eight 107 engine, a frame-mounted sharknose fairing with triple Splitstream vent, dual reflector LED headlamps, linked Brembo ABS and Boom! Box 6.5 GT audio. This is an Ultra model, not the basic Road Glide. Harley-Davidson manufacturer reference ↗ 2024 redesigned Road Glide Harley-Davidson announced a redesigned Road Glide for model year 2024 with the Milwaukee-Eight 117, revised fairing and infotainment. Do not apply the 2024 engine or display specification to earlier Twin Cam or Milwaukee-Eight 107 examples. Harley-Davidson manufacturer reference ↗ What this means for export buyers Give AnyBike a model-year range, complete model designation and preferred factory trim. Identify accessories, non-standard exhausts, infotainment changes and documentation before a price comparison. UK first registration can differ from manufacturer model year.'),
 (143,12,'Documented technical references','road-glide','d9ed17e761080d2076bdd138581f4083cdbd9b6e','technical_specifications','Compare documented specifications','These figures apply only to the labelled manufacturer publications and variants. They are not specifications for every Road Glide model year. UK brochure Road Glide (published edition) Engine Milwaukee-Eight 117 Displacement 1,923 cc Weight 380 kg running order Fuel tank 22.7 litres Harley-Davidson UK brochure Original Harley-Davidson technical source ↗ Market, trim, optional equipment and measurement methods can affect published specifications. Confirm exact VIN and manufacturer model year.'),
 (157,16,'Used buying guidance','street-glide','dc7e9d67bfe9091902029cf76a1ce0c12d6ea404','buying_guidance','UK buyer''s model-specific checklist','Verify Street Glide versus Street Glide Special and the exact factory model code. Check batwing fairing mounts, infotainment, handlebar modifications and speakers. Inspect luggage, rear suspension and signs of heavy touring use. These are suggested inspection points rather than a substitute for a qualified mechanical inspection, HPI checks or verifying export documents.'),
 (157,3,'Model history and production context','street-glide','dc7e9d67bfe9091902029cf76a1ce0c12d6ea404','chronology','Detailed model generations and factory references','Different year-and-trim versions can have different engine families, chassis and touring equipment. These two documented reference points help identify the correct motorcycle before requesting UK supply. 2015 touring-era distinctions Harley-Davidson''s 2015 international lineup distinguishes standard Touring equipment from premium CVO Street Glide, including its upgraded audio system. A CVO should be identified by its complete model code. Harley-Davidson manufacturer reference ↗ 2024 Street Glide FLHX Harley-Davidson''s 2024 factory specification for FLHX lists a 1,923 cc Milwaukee-Eight 117, a six-speed Cruise Drive transmission and belt final drive. These figures describe the 2024 FLHX publication, not all Street Glide motorcycles. Harley-Davidson manufacturer reference ↗ What this means for export buyers Give AnyBike a model-year range, complete model designation and preferred factory trim. Identify accessories, non-standard exhausts, infotainment changes and documentation before a price comparison. UK first registration can differ from manufacturer model year.'),
 (157,12,'Documented technical references','street-glide','dc7e9d67bfe9091902029cf76a1ce0c12d6ea404','technical_specifications','Compare documented specifications','These figures apply only to the labelled manufacturer publications and variants. They are not specifications for every Street Glide model year. UK brochure Street Glide (published edition) Engine Milwaukee-Eight 117 Displacement 1,923 cc Weight 368 kg running order Fuel tank 22.7 litres Harley-Davidson UK brochure Original Harley-Davidson technical source ↗ Market, trim, optional equipment and measurement methods can affect published specifications. Confirm exact VIN and manufacturer model year.'),
 (144,16,'Used buying guidance','road-king','77aed96085c7c7d997c129c9af55f1c7e5076ec6','buying_guidance','UK buyer''s model-specific checklist','Confirm Road King or Road King Special and original trim. Inspect luggage and detachable windshield hardware where fitted. Review wheel finish, chrome or blacked-out parts and originality. These are suggested inspection points rather than a substitute for a qualified mechanical inspection, HPI checks or verifying export documents.'),
 (144,3,'Model history and production context','road-king','77aed96085c7c7d997c129c9af55f1c7e5076ec6','chronology','Detailed model generations and factory references','Different year-and-trim versions can have different engine families, chassis and touring equipment. These two documented reference points help identify the correct motorcycle before requesting UK supply. 1994 Road King introduction The FLHR Road King launched in 1994, bringing classic touring styling to Harley-Davidson''s FL touring chassis. Verify FLHR versus FLHRXS Road King Special before comparing trim, wheels and weather protection. Harley-Davidson manufacturer reference ↗ 2018 Road King versus Road King Special The factory''s 2018 international reference describes distinct Road King and Road King Special variants. The trim, screen fitment, engine package and styling need to be checked against an individual UK motorcycle. Harley-Davidson manufacturer reference ↗ What this means for export buyers Give AnyBike a model-year range, complete model designation and preferred factory trim. Identify accessories, non-standard exhausts, infotainment changes and documentation before a price comparison. UK first registration can differ from manufacturer model year.'),
 (125,16,'Used buying guidance','electra-glide','624a5db19e24c595995818393b55977a0383e7a6','buying_guidance','UK buyer''s model-specific checklist','Confirm the precise FL-series model rather than relying on ''Electra Glide'' alone. Review fairing, luggage, passenger seating and year-dependent electronics. Check maintenance records relevant to the engine and touring chassis generation. These are suggested inspection points rather than a substitute for a qualified mechanical inspection, HPI checks or verifying export documents.'),
 (125,3,'Model history and production context','electra-glide','624a5db19e24c595995818393b55977a0383e7a6','chronology','Detailed model generations and factory references','Different year-and-trim versions can have different engine families, chassis and touring equipment. These two documented reference points help identify the correct motorcycle before requesting UK supply. 1965 electric-start milestone The Electra Glide name dates to the arrival of electric starting in 1965. Over decades, the family has included several FL touring configurations and fairing designs, so the model suffix and year are essential. Harley-Davidson manufacturer reference ↗ 2015 Project RUSHMORE era The Harley-Davidson 2015 European Touring information discusses Project RUSHMORE features and separate Ultra touring configurations. Never describe all Electra Glide variants as having identical rider electronics or engines. Harley-Davidson manufacturer reference ↗ What this means for export buyers Give AnyBike a model-year range, complete model designation and preferred factory trim. Identify accessories, non-standard exhausts, infotainment changes and documentation before a price comparison. UK first registration can differ from manufacturer model year.'),
 (437,16,'Used buying guidance','ultra-limited','ca56fc47f658da253d31a3ddd4b75e7a25a74d20','buying_guidance','UK buyer''s model-specific checklist','Verify Ultra Limited trim, year and engine variant. Test heated grips, infotainment, passenger equipment and touring electrics where fitted. Inspect Tour-Pak, panniers, keys, locks and luggage mounting points. These are suggested inspection points rather than a substitute for a qualified mechanical inspection, HPI checks or verifying export documents.'),
 (437,3,'Model history and production context','ultra-limited','ca56fc47f658da253d31a3ddd4b75e7a25a74d20','chronology','Detailed model generations and factory references','Different year-and-trim versions can have different engine families, chassis and touring equipment. These two documented reference points help identify the correct motorcycle before requesting UK supply. 2015 Ultra Limited Low Harley-Davidson announced the Ultra Limited Low for model year 2015, with a factory seat height of 25.6 inches (about 650 mm), ergonomics for shorter riders and Project RUSHMORE Touring features. This figure is for the Low variant only. Harley-Davidson manufacturer reference ↗ 2018 Touring distinction The 2018 international product guide distinguishes Ultra Limited, Ultra Limited Low and separate CVO touring models. Verify top case, passenger equipment and original electronics against the exact model code. Harley-Davidson manufacturer reference ↗ What this means for export buyers Give AnyBike a model-year range, complete model designation and preferred factory trim. Identify accessories, non-standard exhausts, infotainment changes and documentation before a price comparison. UK first registration can differ from manufacturer model year.'),
 (127,16,'Used buying guidance','fat-boy','32ac86f007fcc480dce46d0dc4cadab72effe930','buying_guidance','UK buyer''s model-specific checklist','Distinguish earlier Softail designs from the substantially revised 2018-on platform. Verify original wheels, tyre sizes, exhaust and engine variant. Inspect modifications to suspension, lighting and registration-compliant equipment. These are suggested inspection points rather than a substitute for a qualified mechanical inspection, HPI checks or verifying export documents.'),
 (127,3,'Model history and production context','fat-boy','32ac86f007fcc480dce46d0dc4cadab72effe930','chronology','Fat Boy: important production generations','Harley-Davidson has reused some model names on very different chassis and engines. These documented milestones distinguish generations; they are not a complete record of every UK specification. 1990 original Fat Boy FLSTF introduced with classic solid-disc-style wheels and Evolution-era Softail architecture. For buyers: Heritage milestone; engine and chassis vary widely across later years. Manufacturer reference ↗ 2018 Fat Boy / Fat Boy 114 Redesigned Softail frame, hidden rear monoshock and Milwaukee-Eight engines; distinct 107/114 variants in the 2018 range. For buyers: Check engine variant and redesigned chassis rather than assuming the classic generation specification. Manufacturer reference ↗ Always confirm VIN, factory model code, production year, engine family, modifications and market-specific homologation.'),
 (115,16,'Used buying guidance','breakout','0c6c42e43d47bc27c71bb262d70aafb317de0c34','buying_guidance','UK buyer''s model-specific checklist','Check FXSB or later model identification and the exact production year. Verify wide rear wheel/tyre specification and originality. Inspect non-standard exhausts, rear fender conversions and steering components. These are suggested inspection points rather than a substitute for a qualified mechanical inspection, HPI checks or verifying export documents.'),
 (115,3,'Model history and production context','breakout','0c6c42e43d47bc27c71bb262d70aafb317de0c34','chronology','Breakout: important production generations','Harley-Davidson has reused some model names on very different chassis and engines. These documented milestones distinguish generations; they are not a complete record of every UK specification. 2013 Breakout model Breakout joined the Softail family with a long, low stance and wide rear wheel. For buyers: Earlier FXSB versions differ from the redesigned Softail range. Manufacturer reference ↗ 2018 Breakout / Breakout 114 Both versions appeared in the redesigned 2018 Softail line with the Milwaukee-Eight engine family. For buyers: Verify FXBR / FXBRS designation, year and original wheel and exhaust equipment. Manufacturer reference ↗ Always confirm VIN, factory model code, production year, engine family, modifications and market-specific homologation.'),
 (430,16,'Used buying guidance','low-rider-s','e1c6b25a40d7203ed7c0a6859414fc60b1d4c363','buying_guidance','UK buyer''s model-specific checklist','Establish the exact model code and generation: earlier Dyna-era versus Softail. Check engine variant, fairing and handlebar equipment for the particular year. Inspect modifications to exhaust, suspension and brakes before comparing prices. These are suggested inspection points rather than a substitute for a qualified mechanical inspection, HPI checks or verifying export documents.'),
 (430,3,'Model history and production context','low-rider-s','e1c6b25a40d7203ed7c0a6859414fc60b1d4c363','chronology','Low Rider S: important production generations','Harley-Davidson has reused some model names on very different chassis and engines. These documented milestones distinguish generations; they are not a complete record of every UK specification. 2016 Dyna Low Rider S The original Low Rider S was a Dyna-platform performance cruiser, not the later Softail Low Rider S. For buyers: Do not compare chassis or factory engine specifications without separating generations. Manufacturer reference ↗ 2020 FXLRS Softail Low Rider S The later Low Rider S appears in Harley-Davidson''s 2020 Softail model family. For buyers: Verify FXLRS identity and original equipment against the production year. Manufacturer reference ↗ Always confirm VIN, factory model code, production year, engine family, modifications and market-specific homologation.'),
 (149,16,'Used buying guidance','softail-standard','3cc1f1dbc0c0fbcc23c911c8a8dd72d495c52111','buying_guidance','UK buyer''s model-specific checklist','Verify model code and Softail platform generation. Confirm whether accessories were factory supplied or added by previous owners. Inspect exhaust, handlebars, wiring and wheel fitments for originality. These are suggested inspection points rather than a substitute for a qualified mechanical inspection, HPI checks or verifying export documents.'),
 (149,3,'Model history and production context','softail-standard','3cc1f1dbc0c0fbcc23c911c8a8dd72d495c52111','chronology','Softail Standard: important production generations','Harley-Davidson has reused some model names on very different chassis and engines. These documented milestones distinguish generations; they are not a complete record of every UK specification. FXST Softail Standard heritage The Softail Standard name has appeared in different eras; historic FXST examples and modern examples should not share an assumed engine specification. For buyers: Use VIN and precise model year to identify factory frame, motor and trim. Manufacturer reference ↗ 2020 Milwaukee-Eight-era Softail Standard The 2020 Softail catalogue identifies a modern Softail Standard as a distinct model. For buyers: Do not infer specifications from other Softail models. Manufacturer reference ↗ Always confirm VIN, factory model code, production year, engine family, modifications and market-specific homologation.'),
 (429,16,'Used buying guidance','iron-883','aa64aa70ce648374ac9afcc926327dfcb2a757fa','buying_guidance','UK buyer''s model-specific checklist','Confirm XL883N model identification and original 883 cc configuration. Inspect corrosion, paint finish, aftermarket exhaust and handlebar conversions. Check service history, tyres and whether UK road equipment remains compliant. These are suggested inspection points rather than a substitute for a qualified mechanical inspection, HPI checks or verifying export documents.'),
 (429,3,'Model history and production context','iron-883','aa64aa70ce648374ac9afcc926327dfcb2a757fa','chronology','Iron 883: documented generations and variants','Harley-Davidson model and trim names can describe different motorcycles over time. The examples below identify specific periods or editions rather than claiming one specification for every year. Traditional XL883N Sportster Air-cooled 883 cc Evolution V-twin, part of the XL Sportster family. Buying guidance: Identify model year and original equipment; this is not a Revolution Max motorcycle. Manufacturer reference ↗ Late production examples Harley-Davidson''s 2022 US line included Iron 883 as a traditional Sportster. Buying guidance: UK availability and final market-specific model years must be confirmed, not inferred from US listings. Manufacturer reference ↗ Match the model year, factory code, market and VIN before using any specification in a purchase or export decision.'),
 (153,16,'Used buying guidance','sportster-s','667f5f40082a442f89ecee03478ae6155437f40c','buying_guidance','UK buyer''s model-specific checklist','Confirm liquid-cooled Revolution Max model identity, not earlier XL Sportster. Check electronic riding systems and service history. Inspect braking system, tyres and accessory changes. Suggested checks; verify documentation, condition and export eligibility independently.'),
 (153,3,'Model history and production context','sportster-s','667f5f40082a442f89ecee03478ae6155437f40c','chronology','Sportster S: documented generations and variants','Harley-Davidson model and trim names can describe different motorcycles over time. The examples below identify specific periods or editions rather than claiming one specification for every year. 2021 introduction Liquid-cooled Revolution Max 1250T engine and modern electronic rider systems. Buying guidance: Significantly different powertrain and chassis from the traditional XL Sportster. Manufacturer reference ↗ 2025 Sportster S Published modern Sportster S specification and equipment should be read against its stated market and year. Buying guidance: Confirm software, riding modes and accessories on individual UK examples. Manufacturer reference ↗ Match the model year, factory code, market and VIN before using any specification in a purchase or export decision.'),
 (431,16,'Used buying guidance','pan-america-1250','bc3f7a27dac481465285723af601347275c9e825','buying_guidance','UK buyer''s model-specific checklist','Confirm Standard, Special or other edition. Do not assume adaptive ride height is fitted. Check wheels, luggage mounts, suspension and service records. Suggested checks; verify documentation, condition and export eligibility independently.'),
 (431,3,'Model history and production context','pan-america-1250','bc3f7a27dac481465285723af601347275c9e825','chronology','Pan America 1250: documented generations and variants','Harley-Davidson model and trim names can describe different motorcycles over time. The examples below identify specific periods or editions rather than claiming one specification for every year. 2021 Pan America launch Liquid-cooled Revolution Max 1250 adventure-touring motorcycle introduced alongside the Pan America 1250 Special. Buying guidance: Special equipment can differ: verify wheel configuration and optional adaptive ride height. Manufacturer reference ↗ 2025 Pan America 1250 ST Road-focused ST variant with 17-inch wheels and its own equipment specification. Buying guidance: Do not describe 1250 ST as the standard adventure Pan America 1250. Manufacturer reference ↗ Match the model year, factory code, market and VIN before using any specification in a purchase or export decision.'),
 (431,12,'Documented technical references','pan-america-1250','bc3f7a27dac481465285723af601347275c9e825','technical_specifications','Compare documented specifications','These figures apply only to the labelled manufacturer publications and variants. They are not specifications for every Pan America 1250 model year. 2025 Pan America 1250 Special (APAC market) Engine Revolution Max 1250 Displacement 1,252 cc Weight 258 kg running order Fuel tank 21.2 litres 2025 manufacturer model specification 2025 Pan America 1250 ST (UK market) Engine Revolution Max 1250 Displacement 1,252 cc Weight 246 kg running order Fuel tank 21.2 litres 2025 manufacturer UK specification Original Harley-Davidson technical source ↗ · 1250 ST UK source ↗ Market, trim, optional equipment and measurement methods can affect published specifications. Confirm exact VIN and manufacturer model year.'),
 (868,16,'Used buying guidance','heritage-classic','3e935cd321067a2c97b0a4ea630f3421f69c6fd3','buying_guidance','UK buyer''s model-specific checklist','Check year and original Softail generation. Inspect windscreen, panniers and attachment hardware. Check original lighting and accessory modifications. Suggested checks; verify documentation, condition and export eligibility independently.'),
 (868,3,'Model history and production context','heritage-classic','3e935cd321067a2c97b0a4ea630f3421f69c6fd3','chronology','Heritage Classic: important production generations','Harley-Davidson has reused some model names on very different chassis and engines. These documented milestones distinguish generations; they are not a complete record of every UK specification. Traditional Heritage Softail Classic Earlier Heritage models combine Softail chassis styling with detachable touring equipment and traditional V-twin engines. For buyers: Check model code, accessories and original generation. Manufacturer reference ↗ 2018 Heritage Classic / Heritage Classic 114 The redesigned 2018 Softail family included separate Heritage Classic and Heritage Classic 114 models. For buyers: Verify luggage, windshield, Milwaukee-Eight version and platform year. Manufacturer reference ↗ Always confirm VIN, factory model code, production year, engine family, modifications and market-specific homologation.'),
 (156,16,'Used buying guidance','street-bob','15e10be1ccb141452586fbb75901dd4d5802c3cd','buying_guidance','UK buyer''s model-specific checklist','Distinguish Dyna and redesigned Softail generations. Verify factory model code and engine. Inspect bars, wiring and aftermarket exhaust. Suggested checks; verify documentation, condition and export eligibility independently.'),
 (156,3,'Model history and production context','street-bob','15e10be1ccb141452586fbb75901dd4d5802c3cd','chronology','Street Bob: important production generations','Harley-Davidson has reused some model names on very different chassis and engines. These documented milestones distinguish generations; they are not a complete record of every UK specification. Pre-2018 Dyna Street Bob Earlier Street Bob models use the Dyna chassis and should not be confused with the revised Softail family. For buyers: Confirm factory model code and suspension layout. Manufacturer reference ↗ 2018 FXBB Street Bob Street Bob moved into Harley-Davidson''s redesigned Softail family for 2018, with a Milwaukee-Eight engine. For buyers: Compare exact chassis and model-year equipment. Manufacturer reference ↗ Always confirm VIN, factory model code, production year, engine family, modifications and market-specific homologation.'),
 (140,16,'Used buying guidance','nightster','9ebe6021fc56c0b0fd7bb32a797f3c8000c10b92','buying_guidance','UK buyer''s model-specific checklist','Confirm Nightster or Nightster Special. Verify electronics, controls and market specification. Inspect maintenance records and modifications. Suggested checks; verify documentation, condition and export eligibility independently.'),
 (140,3,'Model history and production context','nightster','9ebe6021fc56c0b0fd7bb32a797f3c8000c10b92','chronology','Nightster: documented generations and variants','Harley-Davidson model and trim names can describe different motorcycles over time. The examples below identify specific periods or editions rather than claiming one specification for every year. 2022 Nightster introduction Liquid-cooled Revolution Max 975T powertrain, moving away from the earlier XL platform. Buying guidance: Do not confuse Nightster with the earlier XL1200N model bearing the same name. Manufacturer reference ↗ Nightster Special Special variant with revised equipment and electronics; precise features depend on model year. Buying guidance: Verify Nightster versus Nightster Special by factory model designation. Manufacturer reference ↗ Match the model year, factory code, market and VIN before using any specification in a purchase or export decision.'),
 (856,16,'Used buying guidance','v-rod','8fd20f1401cba7aff882d1193b898696d43689f7','buying_guidance','What a UK buyer should check','Verify the exact VRSC variant and year, VIN, cooling system, electrics, fuel system, original exhaust, corrosion, keys and full service history. Check the specific motorcycle''s market homologation and modifications before export.'),
 (856,6,'Model generations','v-rod','8fd20f1401cba7aff882d1193b898696d43689f7','generations','Different V-Rod models and generations','Early VRSCA motorcycles used a 1,130 cc Revolution engine. Later VRSC models introduced a larger 1,250 cc engine and included Night Rod, Night Rod Special, Street Rod and other variants. Don''t apply one model''s tyres, frame geometry, exhaust or suspension specifications to the whole family.'),
 (142,16,'Used buying guidance','pan-america-1250-st','e76fd00f3baba026fad98c433e84f9a664b3cf74','buying_guidance','What a UK buyer should check','Verify the Pan America 1250 ST model designation and year against VIN and V5C. Inspect wheels, tyres, suspension and quickshifter operation. Check electronic aids, ride modes, recalls, service history and available keys. Confirm original equipment, luggage or screen modifications, and destination-country requirements before export.'),
 (142,3,'Model history and production context','pan-america-1250-st','e76fd00f3baba026fad98c433e84f9a664b3cf74','chronology','2025 launch and 2026 development','2025 introduced the Pan America 1250 ST with a Screamin'' Eagle quickshifter, SHOWA suspension, Brembo brakes and road tyres. Harley-Davidson''s 2026 UK publication describes clutchless quickshifting, revised rider modes and Adaptive Ride Height. Confirm the year and standard-versus-optional equipment of any motorcycle offered. Harley-Davidson''s current UK model information is the definitive specification reference for the relevant model year.'),
 (142,12,'Documented technical references','pan-america-1250-st','e76fd00f3baba026fad98c433e84f9a664b3cf74','technical_specifications','2026 UK manufacturer specifications','Engine 1,252 cc Revolution Max 1250, liquid-cooled V-twin Power 150 hp / 112 kW (2026 UK publication) Torque 127 Nm Tyres 120/70ZR17 front; 180/55ZR17 rear, Michelin Scorcher Sport Fuel capacity 21.2 litres Weight 246 kg running order Seat height 825 mm, unladen Values are taken from the manufacturer''s 2026 UK page and should not be assumed to cover all years or export-market variants.'),
 (119,16,'Used buying guidance','cvo-pan-america','a8c48746fd97741ff06b726e2cc9d1d76b4fabb8','buying_guidance','What buyers should check','VIN and exact CVO model designation, not merely CVO accessories Original paint, equipment and fitted luggage Factory recalls, electronics, quickshifter and suspension function Service history, corrosion, crash or off-road damage Number of keys, luggage keys and available documents Verify each motorcycle with its seller before accepting an offer. This is model information, not a condition guarantee.'),
 (119,12,'Documented technical references','cvo-pan-america','a8c48746fd97741ff06b726e2cc9d1d76b4fabb8','technical_specifications','2025 UK-market specifications','1,252 cc liquid-cooled Revolution Max 1250 V-twin Claimed 150 hp (112 kW) and 128 Nm 299 kg in running order (manufacturer figure) Front 19-inch and rear 17-inch tubeless laced wheels Adaptive Ride Height and semi-active suspension Factory quickshifter, protective equipment and premium luggage Figures refer to the 2025 UK specification; individual markets and production years may differ.')
) AS i(model_id,slot,title,slug,revision,category,heading,evidence)
 JOIN public.motorcycle_catalog_models m ON m.id=i.model_id
 WHERE m.manufacturer='Harley-Davidson'
   AND i.slot IN (3,6,12,16) AND length(i.evidence)>=55
   AND length(i.evidence)<=7000 AND i.revision ~ '^[0-9a-f]{40}$';
 IF source_rows<>40 THEN RAISE EXCEPTION 'Harley research source preconditions changed: %',source_rows; END IF;
 SELECT count(*) INTO existing FROM public.motorcycle_universal_page_sections_v1 s
 WHERE s.entity_type='model' AND s.model_id IN (143,157,144,125,437,127,115,430,149,429,153,431,868,156,140,856,142,119);
 IF existing<>18 OR EXISTS(
  SELECT 1 FROM public.motorcycle_universal_page_sections_v1 s
  WHERE s.entity_type='model' AND s.model_id IN (143,157,144,125,437,127,115,430,149,429,153,431,868,156,140,856,142,119)
   AND (s.section_number<>1 OR s.editorial_status<>'draft' OR s.published_at IS NOT NULL)
 ) THEN RAISE EXCEPTION 'Harley research intake stopped: unexpected existing sections'; END IF;
 INSERT INTO public.motorcycle_universal_page_sections_v1
  (entity_type,manufacturer_id,model_id,section_number,section_title,content,
   editorial_status,source_reference,published_at)
 SELECT 'model',NULL,i.model_id,i.slot,i.title,
  jsonb_build_object(
   'summary',i.evidence,
   'source_section_label',i.heading,
   'source_category',i.category,
   'source_verification_status','pending_review',
   'editorial_status','draft',
   'evidence_type','approved_html_excerpt',
   'review_state','source_captured',
   'source_origin','harley-davidson-'||i.slug||'.html',
   'source_revision',i.revision
  ),'draft',
  'harley-davidson-'||i.slug||'.html@'||i.revision,
  NULL
 FROM (VALUES
 (143,16,'Used buying guidance','road-glide','d9ed17e761080d2076bdd138581f4083cdbd9b6e','buying_guidance','UK buyer''s model-specific checklist','Confirm whether it is Road Glide, Road Glide Special, Road Glide Ultra or a CVO variant. Check fairing alignment and whether audio, screen and handlebar modifications are original. Inspect hard panniers, latches, touring electrical equipment and evidence of crash damage. These are suggested inspection points rather than a substitute for a qualified mechanical inspection, HPI checks or verifying export documents.'),
 (143,3,'Model history and production context','road-glide','d9ed17e761080d2076bdd138581f4083cdbd9b6e','chronology','Detailed model generations and factory references','Different year-and-trim versions can have different engine families, chassis and touring equipment. These two documented reference points help identify the correct motorcycle before requesting UK supply. 2017 Road Glide Ultra (FLTRU) The factory''s 2017 Road Glide Ultra specification records a Twin-Cooled Milwaukee-Eight 107 engine, a frame-mounted sharknose fairing with triple Splitstream vent, dual reflector LED headlamps, linked Brembo ABS and Boom! Box 6.5 GT audio. This is an Ultra model, not the basic Road Glide. Harley-Davidson manufacturer reference ↗ 2024 redesigned Road Glide Harley-Davidson announced a redesigned Road Glide for model year 2024 with the Milwaukee-Eight 117, revised fairing and infotainment. Do not apply the 2024 engine or display specification to earlier Twin Cam or Milwaukee-Eight 107 examples. Harley-Davidson manufacturer reference ↗ What this means for export buyers Give AnyBike a model-year range, complete model designation and preferred factory trim. Identify accessories, non-standard exhausts, infotainment changes and documentation before a price comparison. UK first registration can differ from manufacturer model year.'),
 (143,12,'Documented technical references','road-glide','d9ed17e761080d2076bdd138581f4083cdbd9b6e','technical_specifications','Compare documented specifications','These figures apply only to the labelled manufacturer publications and variants. They are not specifications for every Road Glide model year. UK brochure Road Glide (published edition) Engine Milwaukee-Eight 117 Displacement 1,923 cc Weight 380 kg running order Fuel tank 22.7 litres Harley-Davidson UK brochure Original Harley-Davidson technical source ↗ Market, trim, optional equipment and measurement methods can affect published specifications. Confirm exact VIN and manufacturer model year.'),
 (157,16,'Used buying guidance','street-glide','dc7e9d67bfe9091902029cf76a1ce0c12d6ea404','buying_guidance','UK buyer''s model-specific checklist','Verify Street Glide versus Street Glide Special and the exact factory model code. Check batwing fairing mounts, infotainment, handlebar modifications and speakers. Inspect luggage, rear suspension and signs of heavy touring use. These are suggested inspection points rather than a substitute for a qualified mechanical inspection, HPI checks or verifying export documents.'),
 (157,3,'Model history and production context','street-glide','dc7e9d67bfe9091902029cf76a1ce0c12d6ea404','chronology','Detailed model generations and factory references','Different year-and-trim versions can have different engine families, chassis and touring equipment. These two documented reference points help identify the correct motorcycle before requesting UK supply. 2015 touring-era distinctions Harley-Davidson''s 2015 international lineup distinguishes standard Touring equipment from premium CVO Street Glide, including its upgraded audio system. A CVO should be identified by its complete model code. Harley-Davidson manufacturer reference ↗ 2024 Street Glide FLHX Harley-Davidson''s 2024 factory specification for FLHX lists a 1,923 cc Milwaukee-Eight 117, a six-speed Cruise Drive transmission and belt final drive. These figures describe the 2024 FLHX publication, not all Street Glide motorcycles. Harley-Davidson manufacturer reference ↗ What this means for export buyers Give AnyBike a model-year range, complete model designation and preferred factory trim. Identify accessories, non-standard exhausts, infotainment changes and documentation before a price comparison. UK first registration can differ from manufacturer model year.'),
 (157,12,'Documented technical references','street-glide','dc7e9d67bfe9091902029cf76a1ce0c12d6ea404','technical_specifications','Compare documented specifications','These figures apply only to the labelled manufacturer publications and variants. They are not specifications for every Street Glide model year. UK brochure Street Glide (published edition) Engine Milwaukee-Eight 117 Displacement 1,923 cc Weight 368 kg running order Fuel tank 22.7 litres Harley-Davidson UK brochure Original Harley-Davidson technical source ↗ Market, trim, optional equipment and measurement methods can affect published specifications. Confirm exact VIN and manufacturer model year.'),
 (144,16,'Used buying guidance','road-king','77aed96085c7c7d997c129c9af55f1c7e5076ec6','buying_guidance','UK buyer''s model-specific checklist','Confirm Road King or Road King Special and original trim. Inspect luggage and detachable windshield hardware where fitted. Review wheel finish, chrome or blacked-out parts and originality. These are suggested inspection points rather than a substitute for a qualified mechanical inspection, HPI checks or verifying export documents.'),
 (144,3,'Model history and production context','road-king','77aed96085c7c7d997c129c9af55f1c7e5076ec6','chronology','Detailed model generations and factory references','Different year-and-trim versions can have different engine families, chassis and touring equipment. These two documented reference points help identify the correct motorcycle before requesting UK supply. 1994 Road King introduction The FLHR Road King launched in 1994, bringing classic touring styling to Harley-Davidson''s FL touring chassis. Verify FLHR versus FLHRXS Road King Special before comparing trim, wheels and weather protection. Harley-Davidson manufacturer reference ↗ 2018 Road King versus Road King Special The factory''s 2018 international reference describes distinct Road King and Road King Special variants. The trim, screen fitment, engine package and styling need to be checked against an individual UK motorcycle. Harley-Davidson manufacturer reference ↗ What this means for export buyers Give AnyBike a model-year range, complete model designation and preferred factory trim. Identify accessories, non-standard exhausts, infotainment changes and documentation before a price comparison. UK first registration can differ from manufacturer model year.'),
 (125,16,'Used buying guidance','electra-glide','624a5db19e24c595995818393b55977a0383e7a6','buying_guidance','UK buyer''s model-specific checklist','Confirm the precise FL-series model rather than relying on ''Electra Glide'' alone. Review fairing, luggage, passenger seating and year-dependent electronics. Check maintenance records relevant to the engine and touring chassis generation. These are suggested inspection points rather than a substitute for a qualified mechanical inspection, HPI checks or verifying export documents.'),
 (125,3,'Model history and production context','electra-glide','624a5db19e24c595995818393b55977a0383e7a6','chronology','Detailed model generations and factory references','Different year-and-trim versions can have different engine families, chassis and touring equipment. These two documented reference points help identify the correct motorcycle before requesting UK supply. 1965 electric-start milestone The Electra Glide name dates to the arrival of electric starting in 1965. Over decades, the family has included several FL touring configurations and fairing designs, so the model suffix and year are essential. Harley-Davidson manufacturer reference ↗ 2015 Project RUSHMORE era The Harley-Davidson 2015 European Touring information discusses Project RUSHMORE features and separate Ultra touring configurations. Never describe all Electra Glide variants as having identical rider electronics or engines. Harley-Davidson manufacturer reference ↗ What this means for export buyers Give AnyBike a model-year range, complete model designation and preferred factory trim. Identify accessories, non-standard exhausts, infotainment changes and documentation before a price comparison. UK first registration can differ from manufacturer model year.'),
 (437,16,'Used buying guidance','ultra-limited','ca56fc47f658da253d31a3ddd4b75e7a25a74d20','buying_guidance','UK buyer''s model-specific checklist','Verify Ultra Limited trim, year and engine variant. Test heated grips, infotainment, passenger equipment and touring electrics where fitted. Inspect Tour-Pak, panniers, keys, locks and luggage mounting points. These are suggested inspection points rather than a substitute for a qualified mechanical inspection, HPI checks or verifying export documents.'),
 (437,3,'Model history and production context','ultra-limited','ca56fc47f658da253d31a3ddd4b75e7a25a74d20','chronology','Detailed model generations and factory references','Different year-and-trim versions can have different engine families, chassis and touring equipment. These two documented reference points help identify the correct motorcycle before requesting UK supply. 2015 Ultra Limited Low Harley-Davidson announced the Ultra Limited Low for model year 2015, with a factory seat height of 25.6 inches (about 650 mm), ergonomics for shorter riders and Project RUSHMORE Touring features. This figure is for the Low variant only. Harley-Davidson manufacturer reference ↗ 2018 Touring distinction The 2018 international product guide distinguishes Ultra Limited, Ultra Limited Low and separate CVO touring models. Verify top case, passenger equipment and original electronics against the exact model code. Harley-Davidson manufacturer reference ↗ What this means for export buyers Give AnyBike a model-year range, complete model designation and preferred factory trim. Identify accessories, non-standard exhausts, infotainment changes and documentation before a price comparison. UK first registration can differ from manufacturer model year.'),
 (127,16,'Used buying guidance','fat-boy','32ac86f007fcc480dce46d0dc4cadab72effe930','buying_guidance','UK buyer''s model-specific checklist','Distinguish earlier Softail designs from the substantially revised 2018-on platform. Verify original wheels, tyre sizes, exhaust and engine variant. Inspect modifications to suspension, lighting and registration-compliant equipment. These are suggested inspection points rather than a substitute for a qualified mechanical inspection, HPI checks or verifying export documents.'),
 (127,3,'Model history and production context','fat-boy','32ac86f007fcc480dce46d0dc4cadab72effe930','chronology','Fat Boy: important production generations','Harley-Davidson has reused some model names on very different chassis and engines. These documented milestones distinguish generations; they are not a complete record of every UK specification. 1990 original Fat Boy FLSTF introduced with classic solid-disc-style wheels and Evolution-era Softail architecture. For buyers: Heritage milestone; engine and chassis vary widely across later years. Manufacturer reference ↗ 2018 Fat Boy / Fat Boy 114 Redesigned Softail frame, hidden rear monoshock and Milwaukee-Eight engines; distinct 107/114 variants in the 2018 range. For buyers: Check engine variant and redesigned chassis rather than assuming the classic generation specification. Manufacturer reference ↗ Always confirm VIN, factory model code, production year, engine family, modifications and market-specific homologation.'),
 (115,16,'Used buying guidance','breakout','0c6c42e43d47bc27c71bb262d70aafb317de0c34','buying_guidance','UK buyer''s model-specific checklist','Check FXSB or later model identification and the exact production year. Verify wide rear wheel/tyre specification and originality. Inspect non-standard exhausts, rear fender conversions and steering components. These are suggested inspection points rather than a substitute for a qualified mechanical inspection, HPI checks or verifying export documents.'),
 (115,3,'Model history and production context','breakout','0c6c42e43d47bc27c71bb262d70aafb317de0c34','chronology','Breakout: important production generations','Harley-Davidson has reused some model names on very different chassis and engines. These documented milestones distinguish generations; they are not a complete record of every UK specification. 2013 Breakout model Breakout joined the Softail family with a long, low stance and wide rear wheel. For buyers: Earlier FXSB versions differ from the redesigned Softail range. Manufacturer reference ↗ 2018 Breakout / Breakout 114 Both versions appeared in the redesigned 2018 Softail line with the Milwaukee-Eight engine family. For buyers: Verify FXBR / FXBRS designation, year and original wheel and exhaust equipment. Manufacturer reference ↗ Always confirm VIN, factory model code, production year, engine family, modifications and market-specific homologation.'),
 (430,16,'Used buying guidance','low-rider-s','e1c6b25a40d7203ed7c0a6859414fc60b1d4c363','buying_guidance','UK buyer''s model-specific checklist','Establish the exact model code and generation: earlier Dyna-era versus Softail. Check engine variant, fairing and handlebar equipment for the particular year. Inspect modifications to exhaust, suspension and brakes before comparing prices. These are suggested inspection points rather than a substitute for a qualified mechanical inspection, HPI checks or verifying export documents.'),
 (430,3,'Model history and production context','low-rider-s','e1c6b25a40d7203ed7c0a6859414fc60b1d4c363','chronology','Low Rider S: important production generations','Harley-Davidson has reused some model names on very different chassis and engines. These documented milestones distinguish generations; they are not a complete record of every UK specification. 2016 Dyna Low Rider S The original Low Rider S was a Dyna-platform performance cruiser, not the later Softail Low Rider S. For buyers: Do not compare chassis or factory engine specifications without separating generations. Manufacturer reference ↗ 2020 FXLRS Softail Low Rider S The later Low Rider S appears in Harley-Davidson''s 2020 Softail model family. For buyers: Verify FXLRS identity and original equipment against the production year. Manufacturer reference ↗ Always confirm VIN, factory model code, production year, engine family, modifications and market-specific homologation.'),
 (149,16,'Used buying guidance','softail-standard','3cc1f1dbc0c0fbcc23c911c8a8dd72d495c52111','buying_guidance','UK buyer''s model-specific checklist','Verify model code and Softail platform generation. Confirm whether accessories were factory supplied or added by previous owners. Inspect exhaust, handlebars, wiring and wheel fitments for originality. These are suggested inspection points rather than a substitute for a qualified mechanical inspection, HPI checks or verifying export documents.'),
 (149,3,'Model history and production context','softail-standard','3cc1f1dbc0c0fbcc23c911c8a8dd72d495c52111','chronology','Softail Standard: important production generations','Harley-Davidson has reused some model names on very different chassis and engines. These documented milestones distinguish generations; they are not a complete record of every UK specification. FXST Softail Standard heritage The Softail Standard name has appeared in different eras; historic FXST examples and modern examples should not share an assumed engine specification. For buyers: Use VIN and precise model year to identify factory frame, motor and trim. Manufacturer reference ↗ 2020 Milwaukee-Eight-era Softail Standard The 2020 Softail catalogue identifies a modern Softail Standard as a distinct model. For buyers: Do not infer specifications from other Softail models. Manufacturer reference ↗ Always confirm VIN, factory model code, production year, engine family, modifications and market-specific homologation.'),
 (429,16,'Used buying guidance','iron-883','aa64aa70ce648374ac9afcc926327dfcb2a757fa','buying_guidance','UK buyer''s model-specific checklist','Confirm XL883N model identification and original 883 cc configuration. Inspect corrosion, paint finish, aftermarket exhaust and handlebar conversions. Check service history, tyres and whether UK road equipment remains compliant. These are suggested inspection points rather than a substitute for a qualified mechanical inspection, HPI checks or verifying export documents.'),
 (429,3,'Model history and production context','iron-883','aa64aa70ce648374ac9afcc926327dfcb2a757fa','chronology','Iron 883: documented generations and variants','Harley-Davidson model and trim names can describe different motorcycles over time. The examples below identify specific periods or editions rather than claiming one specification for every year. Traditional XL883N Sportster Air-cooled 883 cc Evolution V-twin, part of the XL Sportster family. Buying guidance: Identify model year and original equipment; this is not a Revolution Max motorcycle. Manufacturer reference ↗ Late production examples Harley-Davidson''s 2022 US line included Iron 883 as a traditional Sportster. Buying guidance: UK availability and final market-specific model years must be confirmed, not inferred from US listings. Manufacturer reference ↗ Match the model year, factory code, market and VIN before using any specification in a purchase or export decision.'),
 (153,16,'Used buying guidance','sportster-s','667f5f40082a442f89ecee03478ae6155437f40c','buying_guidance','UK buyer''s model-specific checklist','Confirm liquid-cooled Revolution Max model identity, not earlier XL Sportster. Check electronic riding systems and service history. Inspect braking system, tyres and accessory changes. Suggested checks; verify documentation, condition and export eligibility independently.'),
 (153,3,'Model history and production context','sportster-s','667f5f40082a442f89ecee03478ae6155437f40c','chronology','Sportster S: documented generations and variants','Harley-Davidson model and trim names can describe different motorcycles over time. The examples below identify specific periods or editions rather than claiming one specification for every year. 2021 introduction Liquid-cooled Revolution Max 1250T engine and modern electronic rider systems. Buying guidance: Significantly different powertrain and chassis from the traditional XL Sportster. Manufacturer reference ↗ 2025 Sportster S Published modern Sportster S specification and equipment should be read against its stated market and year. Buying guidance: Confirm software, riding modes and accessories on individual UK examples. Manufacturer reference ↗ Match the model year, factory code, market and VIN before using any specification in a purchase or export decision.'),
 (431,16,'Used buying guidance','pan-america-1250','bc3f7a27dac481465285723af601347275c9e825','buying_guidance','UK buyer''s model-specific checklist','Confirm Standard, Special or other edition. Do not assume adaptive ride height is fitted. Check wheels, luggage mounts, suspension and service records. Suggested checks; verify documentation, condition and export eligibility independently.'),
 (431,3,'Model history and production context','pan-america-1250','bc3f7a27dac481465285723af601347275c9e825','chronology','Pan America 1250: documented generations and variants','Harley-Davidson model and trim names can describe different motorcycles over time. The examples below identify specific periods or editions rather than claiming one specification for every year. 2021 Pan America launch Liquid-cooled Revolution Max 1250 adventure-touring motorcycle introduced alongside the Pan America 1250 Special. Buying guidance: Special equipment can differ: verify wheel configuration and optional adaptive ride height. Manufacturer reference ↗ 2025 Pan America 1250 ST Road-focused ST variant with 17-inch wheels and its own equipment specification. Buying guidance: Do not describe 1250 ST as the standard adventure Pan America 1250. Manufacturer reference ↗ Match the model year, factory code, market and VIN before using any specification in a purchase or export decision.'),
 (431,12,'Documented technical references','pan-america-1250','bc3f7a27dac481465285723af601347275c9e825','technical_specifications','Compare documented specifications','These figures apply only to the labelled manufacturer publications and variants. They are not specifications for every Pan America 1250 model year. 2025 Pan America 1250 Special (APAC market) Engine Revolution Max 1250 Displacement 1,252 cc Weight 258 kg running order Fuel tank 21.2 litres 2025 manufacturer model specification 2025 Pan America 1250 ST (UK market) Engine Revolution Max 1250 Displacement 1,252 cc Weight 246 kg running order Fuel tank 21.2 litres 2025 manufacturer UK specification Original Harley-Davidson technical source ↗ · 1250 ST UK source ↗ Market, trim, optional equipment and measurement methods can affect published specifications. Confirm exact VIN and manufacturer model year.'),
 (868,16,'Used buying guidance','heritage-classic','3e935cd321067a2c97b0a4ea630f3421f69c6fd3','buying_guidance','UK buyer''s model-specific checklist','Check year and original Softail generation. Inspect windscreen, panniers and attachment hardware. Check original lighting and accessory modifications. Suggested checks; verify documentation, condition and export eligibility independently.'),
 (868,3,'Model history and production context','heritage-classic','3e935cd321067a2c97b0a4ea630f3421f69c6fd3','chronology','Heritage Classic: important production generations','Harley-Davidson has reused some model names on very different chassis and engines. These documented milestones distinguish generations; they are not a complete record of every UK specification. Traditional Heritage Softail Classic Earlier Heritage models combine Softail chassis styling with detachable touring equipment and traditional V-twin engines. For buyers: Check model code, accessories and original generation. Manufacturer reference ↗ 2018 Heritage Classic / Heritage Classic 114 The redesigned 2018 Softail family included separate Heritage Classic and Heritage Classic 114 models. For buyers: Verify luggage, windshield, Milwaukee-Eight version and platform year. Manufacturer reference ↗ Always confirm VIN, factory model code, production year, engine family, modifications and market-specific homologation.'),
 (156,16,'Used buying guidance','street-bob','15e10be1ccb141452586fbb75901dd4d5802c3cd','buying_guidance','UK buyer''s model-specific checklist','Distinguish Dyna and redesigned Softail generations. Verify factory model code and engine. Inspect bars, wiring and aftermarket exhaust. Suggested checks; verify documentation, condition and export eligibility independently.'),
 (156,3,'Model history and production context','street-bob','15e10be1ccb141452586fbb75901dd4d5802c3cd','chronology','Street Bob: important production generations','Harley-Davidson has reused some model names on very different chassis and engines. These documented milestones distinguish generations; they are not a complete record of every UK specification. Pre-2018 Dyna Street Bob Earlier Street Bob models use the Dyna chassis and should not be confused with the revised Softail family. For buyers: Confirm factory model code and suspension layout. Manufacturer reference ↗ 2018 FXBB Street Bob Street Bob moved into Harley-Davidson''s redesigned Softail family for 2018, with a Milwaukee-Eight engine. For buyers: Compare exact chassis and model-year equipment. Manufacturer reference ↗ Always confirm VIN, factory model code, production year, engine family, modifications and market-specific homologation.'),
 (140,16,'Used buying guidance','nightster','9ebe6021fc56c0b0fd7bb32a797f3c8000c10b92','buying_guidance','UK buyer''s model-specific checklist','Confirm Nightster or Nightster Special. Verify electronics, controls and market specification. Inspect maintenance records and modifications. Suggested checks; verify documentation, condition and export eligibility independently.'),
 (140,3,'Model history and production context','nightster','9ebe6021fc56c0b0fd7bb32a797f3c8000c10b92','chronology','Nightster: documented generations and variants','Harley-Davidson model and trim names can describe different motorcycles over time. The examples below identify specific periods or editions rather than claiming one specification for every year. 2022 Nightster introduction Liquid-cooled Revolution Max 975T powertrain, moving away from the earlier XL platform. Buying guidance: Do not confuse Nightster with the earlier XL1200N model bearing the same name. Manufacturer reference ↗ Nightster Special Special variant with revised equipment and electronics; precise features depend on model year. Buying guidance: Verify Nightster versus Nightster Special by factory model designation. Manufacturer reference ↗ Match the model year, factory code, market and VIN before using any specification in a purchase or export decision.'),
 (856,16,'Used buying guidance','v-rod','8fd20f1401cba7aff882d1193b898696d43689f7','buying_guidance','What a UK buyer should check','Verify the exact VRSC variant and year, VIN, cooling system, electrics, fuel system, original exhaust, corrosion, keys and full service history. Check the specific motorcycle''s market homologation and modifications before export.'),
 (856,6,'Model generations','v-rod','8fd20f1401cba7aff882d1193b898696d43689f7','generations','Different V-Rod models and generations','Early VRSCA motorcycles used a 1,130 cc Revolution engine. Later VRSC models introduced a larger 1,250 cc engine and included Night Rod, Night Rod Special, Street Rod and other variants. Don''t apply one model''s tyres, frame geometry, exhaust or suspension specifications to the whole family.'),
 (142,16,'Used buying guidance','pan-america-1250-st','e76fd00f3baba026fad98c433e84f9a664b3cf74','buying_guidance','What a UK buyer should check','Verify the Pan America 1250 ST model designation and year against VIN and V5C. Inspect wheels, tyres, suspension and quickshifter operation. Check electronic aids, ride modes, recalls, service history and available keys. Confirm original equipment, luggage or screen modifications, and destination-country requirements before export.'),
 (142,3,'Model history and production context','pan-america-1250-st','e76fd00f3baba026fad98c433e84f9a664b3cf74','chronology','2025 launch and 2026 development','2025 introduced the Pan America 1250 ST with a Screamin'' Eagle quickshifter, SHOWA suspension, Brembo brakes and road tyres. Harley-Davidson''s 2026 UK publication describes clutchless quickshifting, revised rider modes and Adaptive Ride Height. Confirm the year and standard-versus-optional equipment of any motorcycle offered. Harley-Davidson''s current UK model information is the definitive specification reference for the relevant model year.'),
 (142,12,'Documented technical references','pan-america-1250-st','e76fd00f3baba026fad98c433e84f9a664b3cf74','technical_specifications','2026 UK manufacturer specifications','Engine 1,252 cc Revolution Max 1250, liquid-cooled V-twin Power 150 hp / 112 kW (2026 UK publication) Torque 127 Nm Tyres 120/70ZR17 front; 180/55ZR17 rear, Michelin Scorcher Sport Fuel capacity 21.2 litres Weight 246 kg running order Seat height 825 mm, unladen Values are taken from the manufacturer''s 2026 UK page and should not be assumed to cover all years or export-market variants.'),
 (119,16,'Used buying guidance','cvo-pan-america','a8c48746fd97741ff06b726e2cc9d1d76b4fabb8','buying_guidance','What buyers should check','VIN and exact CVO model designation, not merely CVO accessories Original paint, equipment and fitted luggage Factory recalls, electronics, quickshifter and suspension function Service history, corrosion, crash or off-road damage Number of keys, luggage keys and available documents Verify each motorcycle with its seller before accepting an offer. This is model information, not a condition guarantee.'),
 (119,12,'Documented technical references','cvo-pan-america','a8c48746fd97741ff06b726e2cc9d1d76b4fabb8','technical_specifications','2025 UK-market specifications','1,252 cc liquid-cooled Revolution Max 1250 V-twin Claimed 150 hp (112 kW) and 128 Nm 299 kg in running order (manufacturer figure) Front 19-inch and rear 17-inch tubeless laced wheels Adaptive Ride Height and semi-active suspension Factory quickshifter, protective equipment and premium luggage Figures refer to the 2025 UK specification; individual markets and production years may differ.')
) AS i(model_id,slot,title,slug,revision,category,heading,evidence);
 GET DIAGNOSTICS inserted=ROW_COUNT;
 IF inserted<>40 THEN RAISE EXCEPTION 'Harley research insert rollback, wrote %',inserted; END IF;
END $$;
